---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Navid Ahrary"
  description="Background, experience, and career journey of Navid Ahrary, a Cloud and Platform Engineer."
>
  <section class="about">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="page-header">
        <div class="intro-content">
          <p class="section-label">ABOUT</p>

          <h1>
            From telecommunications and backend development to cloud and
            platform engineering.
          </h1>
        </div>

        <div class="profile-image-wrapper">
          <img
            src="/images/profile.jpg"
            alt="Navid Ahrary"
            class="profile-image"
          />
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="content">
        <section>
          <h2>Where I started</h2>

          <p>
            I graduated with a degree in Electrical Engineering -
            Telecommunications. During my studies, however, I became deeply
            interested in IT and web technologies and pursued them alongside my
            academic path.
          </p>

          <p>
            After completing my bachelor's degree and military service in 2017,
            I began teaching myself Linux and earned LPIC-1-level knowledge.
            From there, I moved into algorithms, programming, and web
            development, working primarily with Python and Node.js.
          </p>

          <p>
            During this period, I also explored mobile development with Flutter
            and built several small educational projects. These experiments
            helped me develop a broader understanding of software engineering
            before I focused more seriously on backend and infrastructure work.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Backend development</h2>

          <p>
            My first serious project was a collaboration with a close friend,
            where I worked as a Node.js Backend Developer. At the same time, I
            was responsible for expanding my knowledge of Node.js while also
            dealing with infrastructure and DevOps requirements for the Dongip
            budget management application.
          </p>

          <p>
            I later contributed to several smaller projects as a Backend and
            Web3 Developer. This period gave me practical experience building
            application services, working with different technologies, and
            taking responsibility beyond a narrowly defined development role.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Entering cloud computing</h2>

          <p>
            In 2020, I started my first full-time role as a Node.js Backend
            Developer. Alongside backend development, I gained hands-on
            experience with IoT and Microsoft Azure.
          </p>

          <p>
            This was my entry point into cloud computing. I became involved in
            designing and implementing an Azure-based IoT solution for retail
            stores, supporting customer and operational insights through
            connected devices and cloud services.
          </p>

          <p>
            Working on distributed systems, IoT, and cloud infrastructure
            gradually shifted my focus from application development toward cloud
            engineering and platform architecture.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Building Azure expertise</h2>

          <p>
            To strengthen my cloud knowledge, I earned Microsoft Azure
            certifications including AZ-900, AZ-104, and AZ-204. These
            certifications complemented the practical experience I was gaining
            while designing, building, and operating Azure-based systems.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Cloud engineering today</h2>

          <p>
            Today, I work as an Azure Cloud Engineer, implementing and
            maintaining cloud environments across IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS. My work
            includes Infrastructure as Code with Terraform, automation and
            delivery workflows with Azure DevOps, and the design and operation
            of cloud platforms.
          </p>

          <p>
            I approach cloud engineering with security and cost as fundamental
            engineering constraints. This includes applying least-privilege
            access principles, improving observability, and continuously looking
            for opportunities to optimize cloud resources and operational
            complexity.
          </p>

          <p>
            I also work closely with Cybersecurity and Development teams to
            build cloud environments that are secure, scalable, maintainable,
            and practical to operate.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding: 5rem 0;
  }
  .page-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 220px;
    align-items: start;
    gap: 4rem;

    max-width: 1000px;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .intro-content {
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .profile-image-wrapper {
    width: 220px;
  }

  .profile-image {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;

    object-fit: cover;

    border-radius: 4px;

    filter: grayscale(100%);
  }

  .section-label {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;

    color: var(--accent);

    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .content {
    max-width: 780px;
  }

  .content > section {
    padding: 2.5rem 0;

    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .content > section:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .content h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .content p {
    max-width: 720px;

    color: var(--text-muted);

    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .content p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .about {
      padding: 3.5rem 0;
    }

    .page-header {
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    .content > section {
      padding: 2rem 0;
    }
  }
</style>
